readme='''Integration27 records qualified namespace entry and append-only startup-history handling, plus two portable test-fixture corrections. Public source b66 and runtime source f0 have the same fourteen relevant source/test/ADR paths. Archive bytes are a separate evidence commit and are not a new runtime qualification.\n\nThree normal FIX decisions retain exact CRE DB rows, 177 reproducer records/raw logs and four benchmark records each. The external oracle reproduces the namespace failure on each actual baseline and reports it absent on the corresponding candidate. Failed Git-metadata sandbox probes, original source test failures, the V4 missing-PlantUML environment result with unchanged rerun, and bfe remote 268/270 result remain visible. f0 remote CPU QA actually passed all270 and its own0.362 transport STUB ended with its private server stopped. These overlapping checks are not summed as distinct tests.\n\nRoot subsequently observed actual managed startup READY under a new live development guardian. The original642 UNKNOWN and earlier214 history remain append-only; the exact current acknowledgement is linked to durable CONSUMED and successor INTENT. Private authority, socket, control, nonce, raw environment and complete live telemetry bodies are withheld; their hashes and a selected factual summary are supplied. The firstB attempt then stopped at the external legacy guard before any native run or LLM request. The guard confused the namespace waiter with the owned worker and also required PILOT while the independent production observer was healthy OBSERVE. Loaded Qwen and an active supervisor are not driver or role acceptance. At the recorded observation, two of four attempts and2097152 tokens were charged with usage_unknown preserved; onlyC,D remained. No refill, retry reset, productPASS, task completion, productionACT, safety signoff or endurance result is claimed. Guard repair is separate work.\n\nOperator helper controls use explicit private leaves for ticket validation, historical authority lookup and harmless process effects. They do not mint an owner record or run an actual systemd/cleanup action. Some private fixture companion data stays private; this archive does not claim a fully portable replay of live authority. Normal source gates retain the unchanged evaluator and all175 global prevention cases. Quality-process stdout is retained by the normal evaluator as its recorded digest references, not invented as a separate raw log.\n'''
(RUN/'README.md').write_text(readme)
